(346619, 26770, 8953, '<td valign="top">This is a great shot...I wish the flying man was more of the image</td>', 'This is a great shot...I wish the flying man was more of the image', '2003-07-04 00:55:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(346620, 26966, 5333, '<td valign="top">Cool</td>', 'Cool', '2003-07-04 00:59:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(346621, 27105, 8953, '<td valign="top">nice shot. one of my favorites.the bench to me is a great contrast to the falls in terms of movement and speed.9</td>', 'nice shot. one of my favorites.the bench to me is a great contrast to the falls in terms of movement and speed.9', '2003-07-04 00:59:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(346622, 26648, 8953, '<td valign="top">clever fun shot.</td>', 'clever fun shot.', '2003-07-04 01:03:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(346624, 27175, 6938, '<td valign="top">Nice close up.  I might have tried taking some of the intensity out of the red - but for impact, it works as is.</td>', 'Nice close up.  I might have tried taking some of the intensity out of the red - but for impact, it works as is.', '2003-07-04 01:10:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(346628, 27033, 8911, '<td valign="top">Cute - I could wish you''d been able to get all of the dog more in focus - but I''m impressed that you got as much as you did, since matching any movement is a pain.</td>', 'Cute - I could wish you''d been able to get all of the dog more in focus - but I''m impressed that you got as much as you did, since matching any movement is a pain.', '2003-07-04 01:20:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(346631, 27070, 8911, '<td valign="top">Unfortunately, I''ll have to take your word that this is a ceiling fan. Apparently it was moving fast enough to be completely invisible to your camera, possibly excepting the left-side shadow. This looks like nothing but a slightly blurry photo of a light fixture, to my eyes...not something that gives me an illusion of speed. The yellow-orange cast is also highly distracting.</td>', 'Unfortunately, I''ll have to take your word that this is a ceiling fan. Apparently it was moving fast enough to be completely invisible to your camera, possibly excepting the left-side shadow. This looks like nothing but a slightly blurry photo of a light fixture, to my eyes...not something that gives me an illusion of speed. The yellow-orange cast is also highly distracting.', '2003-07-04 01:24:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(346634, 27031, 8911, '<td valign="top">You could almost convince me that this is a watercolor painting, instead of a photograph. It definitely catches a sense of speed, but I''m not sure the fuzzy nature of it works to its advantage - it looks as if, taken with a bit more care and presented at a higher resolution, it might have looked like a crisp moment-in-time that could have been quite riveting.</td>', 'You could almost convince me that this is a watercolor painting, instead of a photograph. It definitely catches a sense of speed, but I''m not sure the fuzzy nature of it works to its advantage - it looks as if, taken with a bit more care and presented at a higher resolution, it might have looked like a crisp moment-in-time that could have been quite riveting.', '2003-07-04 01:26:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(346638, 26733, 8953, '<td valign="top">This is one of those wow shots! Good job 9</td>', 'This is one of those wow shots! Good job 9', '2003-07-04 01:45:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(346639, 27099, 5333, '<td valign="top">shimano gears, nice</td>', 'shimano gears, nice', '2003-07-04 01:46:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(346640, 27037, 3102, '<td valign="top">Excellent!<br/> <br/>Judging from my extensive knowledge of aircraft, I would have to say that this is a flight of the Viper East Demonstration Team F-16.  And, given the obvious condensation trails pouring off the foreplanes and wingtips, I''d say that this would be consistent with the conditions at the Rhode Island ANG Airshow, Quonset Point.  Also, given that I''m the owner of a D100 myself, I can judge by the subtle nuances of the shot that this photo was also taken with a D100.  Plus I saw the shot with all the details over on PhotoSIG.  :)<br/> <br/>I love the smoke and the red in the afterburner hoodingle (pardon the technical names).  This is just shy of a 10 in my book.  Just a teeny tiny bit more contrast and/or sharpness to bring the jet out a hair more against the sky would be the difference.  Awesome job.  - 9</td>', 'Excellent! Judging from my extensive knowledge of aircraft, I would have to say that this is a flight of the Viper East Demonstration Team F-16.  And, given the obvious condensation trails pouring off the foreplanes and wingtips, I''d say that this would be consistent with the conditions at the Rhode Island ANG Airshow, Quonset Point.  Also, given that I''m the owner of a D100 myself, I can judge by the subtle nuances of the shot that this photo was also taken with a D100.  Plus I saw the shot with all the details over on PhotoSIG.  :) I love the smoke and the red in the afterburner hoodingle (pardon the technical names).  This is just shy of a 10 in my book.  Just a teeny tiny bit more contrast and/or sharpness to bring the jet out a hair more against the sky would be the difference.  Awesome job.  - 9', '2003-07-04 01:52:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(346641, 26612, 9027, '<td valign="top">more effective if car was in motion. :o)</td>', 'more effective if car was in motion. :o)', '2003-07-04 01:53:38.000000', NULL, 1),
