(348445, 27076, 259, '<td valign="top">there''s nothing technically wrong with your photo, and it meets the challenge.  however, it lacks the appeal others have.  generally pictures that do well in the challenges have something to offer that is interesting or appealing outside of just meeting the challenge.</td>', 'there''s nothing technically wrong with your photo, and it meets the challenge.  however, it lacks the appeal others have.  generally pictures that do well in the challenges have something to offer that is interesting or appealing outside of just meeting the challenge.', '2003-07-07 01:02:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(348454, 27105, 259, '<td valign="top">in a weird way it almost looks like a fountain shooting up instead of comming down.  the bench makes this photo much more interesting and adds to the overall perspective which is lost in many photos i see here.  good job.</td>', 'in a weird way it almost looks like a fountain shooting up instead of comming down.  the bench makes this photo much more interesting and adds to the overall perspective which is lost in many photos i see here.  good job.', '2003-07-07 01:05:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(348460, 26988, 259, '<td valign="top">i don''t know the limits to your camera but some blur would help the sense of speed.  as far as composition, the sign above the man''s head takes away from the subject, and balence of the shot.</td>', 'i don''t know the limits to your camera but some blur would help the sense of speed.  as far as composition, the sign above the man''s head takes away from the subject, and balence of the shot.', '2003-07-07 01:08:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(348468, 26887, 259, '<td valign="top">i really like the angled pan, it creates a great diagonal blur.  the biggest thing holding this picture back is the lack of a crisp focus on the truck.</td>', 'i really like the angled pan, it creates a great diagonal blur.  the biggest thing holding this picture back is the lack of a crisp focus on the truck.', '2003-07-07 01:10:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(348469, 26384, 259, '<td valign="top">i like your use of negative space.</td>', 'i like your use of negative space.', '2003-07-07 01:10:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(348474, 26809, 259, '<td valign="top">nice combination of blur and focus overlapping.  i also like the use of a solid background to take away some distractions.  however, by making the background totally black it makes the car seem as though it''s floating which makes the photo seem unstable.</td>', 'nice combination of blur and focus overlapping.  i also like the use of a solid background to take away some distractions.  however, by making the background totally black it makes the car seem as though it''s floating which makes the photo seem unstable.', '2003-07-07 01:14:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(348478, 27180, 259, '<td valign="top">great idea and execution.  i am torn between having fingers in the shot or not having them.  not having them in the shot would help strengthen the subject through having less distractions.  but having them in the shot helps add some realism.  i guess its just a personal preference either way.</td>', 'great idea and execution.  i am torn between having fingers in the shot or not having them.  not having them in the shot would help strengthen the subject through having less distractions.  but having them in the shot helps add some realism.  i guess its just a personal preference either way.', '2003-07-07 01:18:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(348483, 26810, 259, '<td valign="top">i didn''t think that i would see so many dashboard shots in this challenge.  however, yours is probably my favorite.  the first reason is that its the speedometer not the odometer.  and second it''s much more in focus than the others.  not too sure how you were able to shoot the speedometer at almost 80mph with minimal blur, but i guess it could be achieved by jacking the tires or one tire that has the power off the ground and letting it spin freely.</td>', 'i didn''t think that i would see so many dashboard shots in this challenge.  however, yours is probably my favorite.  the first reason is that its the speedometer not the odometer.  and second it''s much more in focus than the others.  not too sure how you were able to shoot the speedometer at almost 80mph with minimal blur, but i guess it could be achieved by jacking the tires or one tire that has the power off the ground and letting it spin freely.', '2003-07-07 01:23:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(348523, 27143, 6900, '<td valign="top">I wouldn''t have cut the two edges of the racket like this, but interesting shot.  Is it a rotation?</td>', 'I wouldn''t have cut the two edges of the racket like this, but interesting shot.  Is it a rotation?', '2003-07-07 01:47:53.000000', NULL, 1),
