(350588, 26729, 9331, '<td valign="top">Didn''t expect this to go so well...<br/>Marbo and Bil99 were the only ones that seemed to pick up on it, but this was cropped from a 6MP image taken on my fuji S602 and the image size pixel for pixel was about 1:1, so the image was seriously noisy (yep it ain''t getting much bigger than what''s displayed without further image degredation). Had to use NeatImage to help clean it up. As such, I really didn''t like the way it affected the water, so didn''t think this would do so well. <br/>This was taken at Manly beach the day after what is known as a "weather bomb" caused huge seas off the coast of Sydney. We had huge waves rolling on to the beaches. I fired off about 150 shots, most of which were dreadful - I had 3 choices that I felt conveyed speed, but this was my favourite. <br/>Thanks for the very appreciated comments :)<br/>By the way - here''s the original image (resized to 640x480), so you can see how much I had to crop to get this<br/><a href="//www.boltdj.com/surf4b.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.boltdj.com/surf4b.jpg</a> <br/>Richard<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-07-09 01:00:16.</i></td>', 'Didn''t expect this to go so well...Marbo and Bil99 were the only ones that seemed to pick up on it, but this was cropped from a 6MP image taken on my fuji S602 and the image size pixel for pixel was about 1:1, so the image was seriously noisy (yep it ain''t getting much bigger than what''s displayed without further image degredation). Had to use NeatImage to help clean it up. As such, I really didn''t like the way it affected the water, so didn''t think this would do so well. This was taken at Manly beach the day after what is known as a "weather bomb" caused huge seas off the coast of Sydney. We had huge waves rolling on to the beaches. I fired off about 150 shots, most of which were dreadful - I had 3 choices that I felt conveyed speed, but this was my favourite. Thanks for the very appreciated comments :)By the way - here''s the original image (resized to 640x480), so you can see how much I had to crop to get this//www.boltdj.com/surf4b.jpg Richard', '2003-07-09 01:10:42.000000', '2003-07-09 02:00:16.000000', 0),
