(351132, 26964, 7531, '<td valign="top">Thank you to all who commented on this photograph, even the negative ones. I knew of course that most would find that it did not meet the challenge and it didn''t at least in an overt way. However, after some consideration I decided that this would be the perfect image for speed as it shows that speed and motion are not always visible and that what we perceive as reality is not always so.<br/> <br/>I took two shots of this girl, this one and one other which are on my web site under black and white - people. <br/> <br/><a href="//www.magicmedia.co.uk" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.magicmedia.co.uk</a> <br/> <br/>Once again thanks for the comments!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-07-09 09:25:03.</i></td>', 'Thank you to all who commented on this photograph, even the negative ones. I knew of course that most would find that it did not meet the challenge and it didn''t at least in an overt way. However, after some consideration I decided that this would be the perfect image for speed as it shows that speed and motion are not always visible and that what we perceive as reality is not always so. I took two shots of this girl, this one and one other which are on my web site under black and white - people.  //www.magicmedia.co.uk  Once again thanks for the comments!', '2003-07-09 10:24:25.000000', '2003-07-09 10:25:03.000000', 0),
(351187, 27037, 3102, '<td valign="top">Wow -- I was being a smartass because I was SURE that you had posted this over at PhotoSIG!  Check out this link and see what I mean...<br/> <br/><a href="//www.photosig.com/go/photos/view?id=957385" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.photosig.com/go/photos/view?id=957385</a> <br/> <br/>I was sure that you had simply cropped this version a little differently, and cleaned it up a bit!<br/> <br/>In any case, congratulations on an awesome image -- I love it!  I was very bummed that the airshow here in Pittsburgh was called off this year.  They decided to nix it back in March as the war was looming over us, and they didn''t know whether they could get the aircraft here.</td>', 'Wow -- I was being a smartass because I was SURE that you had posted this over at PhotoSIG!  Check out this link and see what I mean... //www.photosig.com/go/photos/view?id=957385  I was sure that you had simply cropped this version a little differently, and cleaned it up a bit! In any case, congratulations on an awesome image -- I love it!  I was very bummed that the airshow here in Pittsburgh was called off this year.  They decided to nix it back in March as the war was looming over us, and they didn''t know whether they could get the aircraft here.', '2003-07-09 11:01:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(351254, 27037, 7339, '<td valign="top">Wow Alan, thats too funny. I saw this photographer at the air show. He was about 15 feet to my right. I remember checking out his camera and I think he spotted me too. It was funny really because a young girl behind me commented to her father and I overheard her say, Dad is that camera a digital camera like ours (he had a small point and shoot digital) and he said back to her, no honey, that camera probably costs more then our car. <br/> <br/>I turned at that point and smiled at him. Then showed his family this shot and they were impressed. His son then said he wanted a camera like that and asked if his dad would get him one. He replied, its either that or college. Everyone laughed and we went back to watching the show.<br/></td>', 'Wow Alan, thats too funny. I saw this photographer at the air show. He was about 15 feet to my right. I remember checking out his camera and I think he spotted me too. It was funny really because a young girl behind me commented to her father and I overheard her say, Dad is that camera a digital camera like ours (he had a small point and shoot digital) and he said back to her, no honey, that camera probably costs more then our car.  I turned at that point and smiled at him. Then showed his family this shot and they were impressed. His son then said he wanted a camera like that and asked if his dad would get him one. He replied, its either that or college. Everyone laughed and we went back to watching the show.', '2003-07-09 11:40:11.000000', NULL, 0),
