(355100, 26809, 4285, '<td valign="top">When I saw this I thought this is going to get a ribbon. I gave it an 8, the highest vote I cast in the challenge. I certainly didn''t think mine could possibly beat this great entry. There''s surely no accounting for taste. Cheers.<br/> <br/>Owen</td>', 'When I saw this I thought this is going to get a ribbon. I gave it an 8, the highest vote I cast in the challenge. I certainly didn''t think mine could possibly beat this great entry. There''s surely no accounting for taste. Cheers. Owen', '2003-07-13 10:00:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(355204, 27059, 5112, '<td valign="top">FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB<br/> <br/>Hello,<br/> <br/>I like this picture very much, the colours, shapes, the crop, everything is very beautiful.  But, like a couple of your commenters below, I am not making the connection to "Speed", unless I think of speed as movement, and you are depicting the camera''s movement here.  <br/> <br/>It is a beautiful picture though.  The yellows, oranges and blues are very clean, as is the movement.  Technically I can find no fault with it.<br/> <br/>As a composition it is very interesting, especially on second (or third ...) look.  At first I think the reaction is, "Oh, just another long exposure."  But on looking again, the building to the right becomes visible, the dark sky to the left.  After that I start to see shapes, and the picture becomes a sexy abstract, at times an almost scary abstract.  To the right there''s a woman, bending backwards a little, as if she''s trying to get away from something, possibly the big thing in the middle.  The middle also looks like a being, but I can''t tell the gender, and it''s a frightening being.  But I''m letting my imagination get away here.  <br/> <br/>Anyway.  I like this picture.  I think it didn''t do better in the challenge because it doesn''t come out and hit you, "THIS IS SPEED!!!".  Your picture, though beautiful, is out of the norm.  I like a lot of your pictures - you have quite a style!<br/> <br/>Ursula (uabresch)<br/>Comments, questions, complaints ... feel free to contact me.</td>', 'FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB Hello, I like this picture very much, the colours, shapes, the crop, everything is very beautiful.  But, like a couple of your commenters below, I am not making the connection to "Speed", unless I think of speed as movement, and you are depicting the camera''s movement here.   It is a beautiful picture though.  The yellows, oranges and blues are very clean, as is the movement.  Technically I can find no fault with it. As a composition it is very interesting, especially on second (or third ...) look.  At first I think the reaction is, "Oh, just another long exposure."  But on looking again, the building to the right becomes visible, the dark sky to the left.  After that I start to see shapes, and the picture becomes a sexy abstract, at times an almost scary abstract.  To the right there''s a woman, bending backwards a little, as if she''s trying to get away from something, possibly the big thing in the middle.  The middle also looks like a being, but I can''t tell the gender, and it''s a frightening being.  But I''m letting my imagination get away here.   Anyway.  I like this picture.  I think it didn''t do better in the challenge because it doesn''t come out and hit you, "THIS IS SPEED!!!".  Your picture, though beautiful, is out of the norm.  I like a lot of your pictures - you have quite a style! Ursula (uabresch)Comments, questions, complaints ... feel free to contact me.', '2003-07-13 12:52:15.000000', NULL, 0),
