(633789, 26733, 16362, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by UberFish:</b></div><hr/><i> From your comment, it seems you dont realise that this is a hoverfly (Episyrphus balteatus), and is in the same order (Diptera) as houseflies and fruit flies, rather than the bees-wasps-ants order (Hymenoptera). A wasp on the wing would be *really* hard to capture, as they dont hang about and spend hardly any time at all at each flower. Congrats on a top 10 place. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>LOL</td>', 'Originally posted by UberFish: From your comment, it seems you dont realise that this is a hoverfly (Episyrphus balteatus), and is in the same order (Diptera) as houseflies and fruit flies, rather than the bees-wasps-ants order (Hymenoptera). A wasp on the wing would be *really* hard to capture, as they dont hang about and spend hardly any time at all at each flower. Congrats on a top 10 place.  LOL', '2004-03-23 16:33:25.000000', NULL, 0),
